If more than one `UnitType` is passed to the func, you mean? True.

Since xorm doesn't seem to have a `FindDistinct()` func I could use instead of 

```go
return ids, sess.Where("owner_id = ?", u.ID).Find(&ids)
```
... the only thing I can think of is explicitly clearing duplicates from `ids` before I return them, like so:

```go
idsWithDuplicates, err := sess.Where("owner_id = ?", u.ID).Find(&idsWithDuplicates)
keys := make(map[int]bool)
ids := []int{}
for _, entry := range idsWithDuplicates {
    if _, value := keys[entry]; !value {
        keys[entry] = true
        ids = append(ids, entry)
    }
}  
return ids, err
```

Somehow I think there must be a better way. Any suggestions on how to handle that more elegantly?
